From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: emit bounded logs as each SoftHSM test fails

The complete SoftHSM suite exceeded the target CI's 180-minute budget after
several RSA tests had already failed. Automake wrote the individual failure
logs in the build tree, but the run timeout prevented its final summary from
reaching the uploaded build log. Emit the last 200 lines of each failed test
immediately after its result is known. Do not alter the test invocation,
result classification, test list, or make check exit status.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI run 36424142097 and the upstream
 Automake test-driver included in libp11 0.4.21
Patch-License: GPL-2.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
Remove-When: Target CI captures individual failed test logs before timeout.
---
diff --git a/test-driver b/test-driver
--- a/test-driver
+++ b/test-driver
@@ -143,6 +143,15 @@
 # Report outcome to console.
 echo "${col}${res}${std}: $test_name"
-
+case $res in
+  FAIL|ERROR|XPASS)
+    echo "--- $test_name diagnostic log (last 200 lines) ---"
+    if test -r "$log_file"; then
+      tail -n 200 "$log_file"
+    fi
+    echo "--- end $test_name diagnostic log ---"
+    ;;
+esac
+
 # Register the test result, and other relevant metadata.
 echo ":test-result: $res" > $trs_file
 echo ":global-test-result: $res" >> $trs_file
